.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:1:# ISSUE-014 — Agent-estimated goal progress percentage
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:10:Next best session: implement optional advisory progress estimates for pi-goals
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:11:Next best session rationale: State ownership, update semantics, UI rendering, safety-counter behavior, and proof shape are now locked.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:12:Target repo roots: `~/dev/personal/experiments/pi-goals`
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:13:Parent issue: `.ai/issues/fixed/ISSUE-001-pi-goal-extension.md`
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:14:Depends on: `.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-011-goal-widget-real-component-and-narrow-width.md`
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:15:Related: `.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-021-goal-completion-proofs.md`, `.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-024-goal-audit-command.md`
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:19:Add optional agent-updated progress estimates to persistent goals, with instant reactive UI when used and no UI clutter when unused.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:21:The estimate is advisory metadata only. It must not complete a goal, satisfy completion proofs, bypass audit/proof gates, or reset no-progress safety counters by itself.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:25:The runtime tracks objective, status, usage, budgets, completion floors, and internal telemetry, but it has no user-facing progress estimate. For long-running goals, users may ask the working agent to periodically estimate progress such as `35%` with a short rationale.
