.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:55:- Current `lifecycle.ts` counts any successful `update_goal` result with a `goal` object as productive turn progress; this must be refined so progress-only updates do not defeat no-progress safety.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:62:Add optional progress estimate fields to `GoalState`:
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:65:progressPercent?: number;
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:66:progressNote?: string;
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:67:progressUpdatedAt?: number;
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:70:Do not store first-pass progress estimates in telemetry or a separate event stream.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:74:Add `update_goal` params:
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:76:- `progress_percent?: number | null`
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:77:- `progress_note?: string | null`
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:81:- `progress_percent` must be an integer `0..100` or `null`;
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:82:- `progress_note` must trim to at most 160 characters;
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:84:- `progress_percent: null` clears the whole estimate;
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:85:- note-only updates are rejected unless an estimate already exists;
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:86:- no-op progress updates are rejected.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:90:- `progress_percent: 100` is allowed but remains `est 100%`.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:91:- A progress estimate never changes goal status.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:102:- `/goal`, `get_goal`, and `update_goal` output include `Progress estimate: <percent>%` plus note when present;
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:103:- framed widget mode adds one conditional progress row after the objective row;
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:104:- compact widget mode adds one conditional progress row after the status/objective row;
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:107:No stale/expired visual styling in first release. Store `progressUpdatedAt` for future use.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:111:Progress-only `update_goal` calls must not count as productive work for no-progress safety counters.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:113:Implementation should expose structured update metadata from `update_goal` so lifecycle can distinguish progress-only changes from substantive status/objective/budget/floor changes.
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:119:| Store in telemetry | User-facing estimate should replay with goal state and appear in goal details. |
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:120:| Add separate progress stream first | Current state events already provide branch-local persistence and reactive UI. |
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:121:| Require notes for every update | Too heavy for quick estimates; optional bounded note is enough. |
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:122:| Restrict active goals to `0..99` | `100` can be useful as a subjective estimate; completion gates remain authoritative. |
.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-014-goal-progress-estimates.md:124:| Count progress-only updates as progress | Would let agents avoid no-progress safety by changing subjective estimates. |
