README.md:1:# pi-goals
README.md:3:Persistent goal tracking for [Pi](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent). Inspired by Codex CLI's `/goal`, `pi-goals` adds Pi-native UX, rewindable `/tree`-compatible goal state, time and token budgets, reusable token-aware prompts, automated churn monitoring, and more.
README.md:5:> Early preview: `pi-goals` is usable, but install ergonomics and APIs may change before `1.0.0`.
README.md:9:- `/goal` command for creating, pausing, resuming, replacing, and clearing a persistent objective.
README.md:11:- Time and token budgets with goal-aware continuation and wrap-up behavior.
README.md:12:- Optional completion floors that prevent premature wrap-up until minimum goal-directed work has happened.
README.md:13:- Reusable token-aware prompt templates from `.pi-goals/` directories.
README.md:14:- Durable FIFO goal queue for sequential goal work.
README.md:15:- Queue-aware model tools for listing, enqueuing, starting, dequeuing, and removing queued goals.
README.md:16:- Natural-language reusable prompt discovery via `list_goal_templates` and `create_goal_from_template`.
README.md:17:- Model tools for inspecting and updating the active goal.
README.md:18:- Automated churn monitoring and steering for long-running goals.
README.md:26:pi install npm:pi-goals
README.md:32:pi install -l npm:pi-goals
README.md:35:## `/goal` command
README.md:37:Use `/goal` to create and manage a persistent objective that survives across turns and is persisted into the Pi branch so `/tree` rewind/replay semantics stay coherent.
README.md:40:/goal
README.md:41:/goal <objective>
README.md:42:/goal queue
README.md:43:/goal queue <objective-or-template>
README.md:44:/goal pause
README.md:45:/goal resume
README.md:46:/goal clear
README.md:51:- `/goal` — show the current goal summary, status, budgets, and progress metadata.
README.md:52:- `/goal <objective>` — create a new active goal. If a goal already exists, Pi asks before replacing it.
README.md:53:- `/goal queue` — list queued goals.
README.md:54:- `/goal queue <objective-or-template>` — enqueue a direct objective or reusable template invocation for later.
README.md:55:- `/goal pause` — pause continuation and churn monitoring. If a goal-driven turn is active, Pi interrupts it.
README.md:56:- `/goal resume` — resume a paused goal and schedule continuation/monitoring again.
README.md:57:- `/goal clear` — remove the current goal from active state.
README.md:59:The extension also exposes model tools so agents can inspect, create, update, pause, resume, complete, clear, or queue goals without string-parsing the slash command.
README.md:63:`pi-goals` supports a durable FIFO queue for sequential work. Queued goals are persisted into the Pi branch alongside goal state, so replay and `/tree` semantics remain coherent.
README.md:66:/goal queue
README.md:67:/goal queue write the release notes
README.md:68:/goal queue fix-issue --issue ISSUE-123 -- verify the fix
README.md:73:- `list_goal_queue`
README.md:74:- `enqueue_goal`
README.md:75:- `start_queued_goal`
README.md:76:- `dequeue_goal`
README.md:77:- `remove_queued_goal`
README.md:79:For queued prose that looks like a reusable workflow, agents can list templates with `list_goal_templates`, create a concrete goal with `create_goal_from_template`, then dequeue the original queue item after the concrete goal is satisfied.
README.md:81:## Natural language goal management
README.md:83:You do not have to use explicit `/goal` commands for every operation. Because `pi-goals` exposes goal management as Pi model tools, the Pi agent can manage goals from ordinary natural language instructions.
README.md:88:Keep working toward shipping this release, but pause the persistent goal while I answer email.
README.md:92:Set a goal to finish the README cleanup with a 30 minute budget, then keep going until it is done or blocked.
README.md:96:Mark the current goal complete and summarize what changed.
README.md:99:Use `/goal` when you want direct command control; use natural language when you want the agent to decide the right goal operation in context.
README.md:101:When a goal reaches its time or token budget, `pi-goals` steers the agent into wrap-up instead of silently continuing. Exhausted goals cannot be resumed until the budget is raised or the goal is cleared.
README.md:105:Model tools can set optional minimum work floors when creating or updating a goal:
README.md:107:- `min_tokens_before_wrap_up`
README.md:108:- `min_time_seconds_before_wrap_up`
README.md:110:These are completion floors, not quota targets. If an agent calls `update_goal({ status: "complete" })` before configured floors are met, completion is deferred, the goal remains active, and the tool returns structured `completion_blocked_by_floor`, floor deltas, and a concrete `next_floor_pass` from the value-pass catalog. Steering asks for one objective-linked improvement pass such as requirement-gap audit, validation expansion, adversarial review, simplification/deslop, compatibility review, or docs/handoff evidence.
README.md:112:Maximum budgets still win: budget-limited goals wrap up rather than working past a cap to satisfy a floor. Users can remove or lower a floor with `update_goal`, but floor edits and `status: "complete"` must be separate calls.
README.md:114:## Reusable `.pi-goals` prompts
README.md:116:`pi-goals` can turn project prompt templates into reusable goal objectives. Put Markdown, `.markdown`, or `.txt` templates under any `.pi-goals/` directory in your workspace:
README.md:119:.pi-goals/
README.md:124:Then invoke a template by name through `/goal`:
README.md:127:/goal fix-issue --issue ISSUE-123 -- verify the fix and update docs
README.md:128:/goal release/checklist --version 0.1.1
README.md:152:Reusable templates are available to both slash commands and model tools. Agents can call `list_goal_templates` to discover templates and `create_goal_from_template` to create a concrete goal from one. Template invocations also work through `/goal queue`.
README.md:156:Long-running goals can drift, loop, or stall. `pi-goals` runs a lightweight goal-scoped churn monitor that periodically reviews sparse session context, recent goal telemetry, recent completion-floor state, and recent monitor decisions.
README.md:160:- detect no-progress loops and repeated automatic turns,
README.md:166:Monitor state is goal-scoped and replayable, so branching and `/tree` operations stay aligned with the active goal history.
README.md:172:npm run quality:goal
README.md:175:`npm run quality:goal` runs the project quality gate for the extension, including [Sentrux](https://github.com/sentrux/sentrux) structure checks, TypeScript validation, and Pi extension load validation.
